{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"239dc5b975db8d12","type":"group","x":-100,"y":-380,"width":996,"height":329,"color":"3","label":"Epoch II"},
		{"id":"c7f0575d7cc63fe3","type":"group","x":512,"y":121,"width":531,"height":616,"color":"2","label":"EPOCH III"},
		{"id":"5c3c5ac23fd9af83","type":"group","x":-680,"y":120,"width":910,"height":280,"color":"1","label":"Epoch I"},
		{"id":"2b531735f4396792","type":"text","text":"# Planck Epoch (t = 0-10$^{-43}$)\n- The **\"earliest phase\"** of the universe \n- The Four Fundamental Forces (gravity, strong and weak nuclear, electromagnetism) are unified\n- Ends when gravity separates from the other forces\n","x":-660,"y":140,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"cc9c75f606b29066","type":"text","text":"# Singularity Point (t=0)\n- Point where there was nothing but the singularity — **an infinitely small, dense, and hot point** \n- This point **breaks our current law of physics** \n\n","isStartNode":false,"x":-660,"y":-220,"width":400,"height":200},
		{"id":"c42ee6bc0ba7bfff","type":"text","text":"# Inflationary Epoch (t = 10$^{-36}$-10$^{-32}$)\n- Universe starts to expand exponentially \n- Smooths the universe into **near-uniformity**\n> [!seealso]\n>  [[The Universe — Origin Theories#Inflation Theory]] ","x":-80,"y":-360,"width":440,"height":280},
		{"id":"af9a4119eaee4603","type":"text","text":"# Electroweak Epoch  (t = 10$^{-32}$-10$^{-12}$)\n- Weak and strong electromagnetic forces separate from each other\n- Universe cools to ~10¹⁵ K; **matter-antimatter asymmetry begins .**","x":400,"y":-360,"width":471,"height":283},
		{"id":"e094f8c5ee37f41d","type":"text","text":"# Grand Unification Epoch (t = 10$^{-43}$-10$^{-36}$)\n- Fundamental Particles (quarks, leptons) begin to emerge\n-  Ends when strong nuclear force separates, triggering the inflationary epoch ","x":-180,"y":140,"width":390,"height":240},
		{"id":"6675ab9f6b038922","type":"text","text":"# 5. Quark Epoch  (t = 10⁻¹² to 10⁻⁶ ) \n- Quarks, electrons, and neutrinos dominate.  \n- Matter and antimatter annihilate, leaving a slight excess of matter (1 quark per billion pairs).  \n- Ends when quarks combine to form hadrons (protons, neutrons) .","x":532,"y":141,"width":491,"height":243},
		{"id":"ba92da1c9aaaad08","type":"text","text":"","x":533,"y":494,"width":488,"height":210}
	],
